# Auto conventional commits

This project rule **overrides** “only commit when asked”: in this repo the agent **must** commit after finishing work, before the final reply.

## When to commit

1. After each **completed logical unit of work** (feature, fix, refactor slice, docs/rules change) — not one mega-commit for unrelated things.
2. **Before** ending the assistant turn / final user-facing answer for that work.
3. If several independent changes landed in one turn, make **several** commits (logical split), then answer.

## Commit style

- **Conventional Commits**: `feat|fix|refactor|docs|chore|style|test|perf(scope?): subject`
- Userscripts: follow `userscript-versioning.mdc` — bump `@version` and put `(vX.Y.Z)` in the subject when a `.user.js` changed.
- HEREDOC for the message; no `--no-verify`; no force push; no amend unless the user’s amend rules allow it.
- Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials). Do not commit unless there are real changes.

## End of reply

After commits, include a short line (or list) with **short hash + full subject** for each new commit, e.g.:

`a1b2c3d feat(hide-elements): TM menu toggles (v2.0.0)`

If nothing to commit (clean tree), say so briefly — do not create an empty commit.

## Push

Push only when the user asks (or an existing explicit project habit for that task). Committing ≠ pushing.
